+The strict explicit TensorIR producer copies compute capability and SM count.
+It disables automatic candidate search, so pinned TensorIR's cc>=100
+shared-memory assumption in tile candidate generation is not used. Default and
+opt-in CTA shared-memory limits, block/grid limits, register limits, and other
+resource traits are deliberately not claimed as producer options yet. A future
+loader/legality gate must consume those traits and inspect the generated kernel
+resources before launch. Until that gate lands, this object and Artifact v1 are
+target identity/capability plus compiled-byte and callable-ABI data, not proof
+that a generated launch is legal.
 
 This contract does not query CUDA, link TensorIR/CUDA Tile, compile an
 artifact, or launch a kernel.
