+The source API is bytes-only. PyPTO validates a non-empty, NUL-free sequence of
+at most 16 MiB, hashes those exact owned bytes, checks the build-specification
+digest before invoking TensorIR, and compiles that same byte sequence. It does
+not perform Unicode decoding or parse/print normalization.
+
+The compiled backend identity and producer result are not arguments.
+`ArtifactProducerIdentity` is read-only, and neither a public producer-result
+constructor nor `create_strict()` exists. `compile_strict()` obtains the private
+build anchor and invokes the concrete runtime-free TensorIR producer internally.
+The producer toolchain must match the compiled PyPTO, TensorIR, CUDA Tile, LLVM,
+CUDA toolkit, and `tileiras` identities exactly. Backend-OFF builds still expose
+the data model and source-digest API, but compilation fails closed.
+
+Compilation releases the Python GIL but is serialized because concurrent
+TensorIR compilation is not accepted yet. The first producer attempt claims the
+current process. A child that inherits PyPTO through `fork()` after that point
+is rejected before taking the inherited mutex; serving workers must be created
+with spawn/exec, or forked before any producer attempt, and compile inside each
+worker.
 
